WEBVTT

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:48.880
We're leaving, Soichiro.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:02.440
I'm not moving out,
Manager. I won't go.

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:17.920
What?!

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:22.270
Manager left? No way!

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:23.420
She's gone.

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:25.900
It must be your fault.

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:30.560
Since she took Soichiro,
she could be gone for good.

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:34.010
Maybe she couldn't
bear to stay.

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:37.270
After all, the guy she thought she
had wrapped around her finger

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:38.710
proposed to another woman.

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:39.900
That's not what happened!

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:41.770
So, what happened?

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:45.110
It's just that Kozue.

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:55.150
So do you get it now?

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.930
How long are you
going to sit there?

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:05.860
Go get her.

00:03:07.210 --> 00:03:08.050
But.

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:10.560
I said, go get her!

00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:11.930
Yes!

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:16.710
You're not stepping
back in here

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:19.400
unless you bring back
the manager!

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.080
He's let his guard down now that
Mitaka is out of the picture.

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:28.180
Are those two ever
going to get together?

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:33.680
What's the matter, Kyoko?
Why did you bring the dog?

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:35.960
You can't keep him in here.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:37.960
Take him
out to the patio.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:39.700
He's going to
mess up the house.

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:42.740
Please! Be nicer
to him, will you?

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:45.210
He's going to be a part
of your family for a while.

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:48.980
You moved out
of that place?

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:57.240
You're going to quit
being the manager?

00:03:57.520 --> 00:03:59.150
I don't know.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:03.200
I knew you'd be better
off marrying Mitaka.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:06.960
You're a widow who's
not so young anymore,

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:08.960
with no advanced
degree or skills.

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:11.480
I don't know if you'll
ever find another man

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:14.070
who'd be willing
to marry you.

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:17.830
Do you enjoy insulting
your own daughter?

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:19.510
Let me set you up.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:21.270
Don't jump the gun.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:25.210
I'm only thinking
about your happiness.

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:27.060
I'm not getting married.

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:28.390
Oh, you.

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:31.210
I'll never get married!

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:36.940
Calm down!

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:41.660
But...! But you proposed
to me, Godai!

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:43.440
That jerk!

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:45.940
He dumped you because
you were dilly-dallying.

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:50.170
I dumped HIM! He's so
irresponsible and clueless.

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:54.310
Mitaka was very clear
with his intentions.

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:56.080
Who do you think
I'm talking about?

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:59.710
Who? Who are you
talking about?

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:05.020
Are you in love
with someone?

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:13.530
Hey! Kyoko!
If there is someone..

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:16.830
Yes?!

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:26.160
Yes?

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:27.400
Hello.

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:29.750
You're from...

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:32.390
Maison Ikkoku.

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:35.340
I'm Godai, Mrs. Chigusa.

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:36.620
Godai?

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:38.920
Yes, Kyoko is here.

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:40.690
Just a minute, please.

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:43.890
Kyoko, a man
named Godai is here.

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:45.070
Tell him to leave.

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:47.940
But.

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:50.370
Just tell him to leave.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:05:59.170
I'm sorry.

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:02.840
She's not feeling well

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:05.020
I see.

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:08.650
Excuse me.

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:13.460
Kyoko! Please just listen!

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:15.090
Last night was
a misunderstanding!

00:06:15.530 --> 00:06:17.440
I never proposed to her!

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:19.900
She misunderstood me, and-

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:25.570
Hi.

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:30.380
Get out!
How low can you get?!

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:31.970
K-Kyoko!

00:06:32.210 --> 00:06:34.450
I don't even want to hear
a dumb excuse like that!

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:35.780
W-Wait!

00:06:50.030 --> 00:06:54.590
Kyoko? Was that the man
you're in love with?

00:06:55.510 --> 00:06:56.560
No way.

00:06:58.250 --> 00:06:59.870
I can't be bothered
with a jerk like that.

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:02.090
What was his name?

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:06.600
It's Godai! When
will you ever learn?!

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:12.310
I better learn it now.

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:26.330
I guess I better
give her some time.

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:35.600
This is totally
unlike the manager.

00:07:35.950 --> 00:07:37.840
She's abandoned
her duties.

00:07:38.210 --> 00:07:41.310
Akemi! Please get to work.

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:44.830
Shut up! This is important.

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:47.190
Master! Where's our
wiener and smelt?

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:48.880
Just a minute, please.

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:51.900
She totally lacks
the responsibility

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:53.870
of a career woman.

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:57.420
She could use some
stress-free time off.

00:07:58.140 --> 00:08:02.330
Meanwhile, we can party
and live rent-free.

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:07.830
But there's a very complex
reason behind her leaving.

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:10.970
We have to
be understanding.

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:14.150
Welcome home.

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:16.650
Is Kyoko still here?

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:18.750
She didn't go back to
Maison Ikkoku, did she?

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:20.780
No, she's here
to stay for a while.

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:22.120
Good. Good.

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:25.630
Kyoko! I brought back
something for you!

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:33.390
Aren't these great?

00:08:33.640 --> 00:08:36.000
You're such a softy.

00:08:36.610 --> 00:08:39.340
Don't you care to know why
she left that apartment house?

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:43.350
Never mind. You stay
as long as you want.

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:46.400
It's not a problem
for me to support you.

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:48.010
Thanks, Dad.

00:08:49.150 --> 00:08:51.810
You quit your job,
you refuse remarry.

00:08:52.150 --> 00:08:53.520
What do you plan
to do now?

00:08:55.150 --> 00:08:55.990
What was
that man's name?

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:57.620
The one who came to
see you this afternoon?

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:02.240
Who's this?! I never
heard about such a man!

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:04.260
You know, he's
from Maison Ikkoku.

00:09:04.430 --> 00:09:07.000
You've seen him
many times, Dad.

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:10.060
I have? What's he like?

00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:13.270
What's his occupation?
How old is he?

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:15.510
Is he educated?
How's his personality?

00:09:17.310 --> 00:09:20.570
Stop it. He's nothing to me.
I'm going to bed.

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:23.010
Bed? Kyoko!

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:24.040
Kyoko!

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:31.910
So who's the man who came
to see her this afternoon?

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:34.120
There's something going on.

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:36.230
Something? Like what?

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:40.970
Nothing, really...
but something.

00:09:43.570 --> 00:09:45.800
Maybe perhaps something.

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:49.060
What do you mean?

00:09:49.990 --> 00:09:52.030
I don't approve of him!

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:54.850
If he shows up again,
I'll chase him away.

00:09:57.230 --> 00:09:59.680
They just love to
jump to conclusions.

00:10:15.070 --> 00:10:16.560
Marriage, marriage...

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:19.530
That's all I hear about.

00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:31.650
Remarriage...

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:38.260
He's scum, don't you think?

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:46.600
I won't go back, even if he
comes back a hundred times!

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:03.070
It's locked.

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:08.150
You're not stepping back in here
unless you bring back Manager!

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:13.630
Why, you...!

00:11:14.030 --> 00:11:15.230
Get up!

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:17.050
Hey! Open up!

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:22.370
C'mon! Open up!

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:25.190
Damn!

00:11:36.020 --> 00:11:37.860
She wouldn't be back.

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:42.220
Kentaro, open up.

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:50.500
Brother Godai? What's up?

00:11:50.840 --> 00:11:52.660
Never mind. Just open up.

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:55.100
What's going on?

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:58.010
How dare they lock me out.

00:11:58.070 --> 00:11:59.190
No! Don't!

00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:04.170
Brother Godai?!

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:06.340
Ouch!

00:12:07.020 --> 00:12:08.770
That's why I tried
to stop you.

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:10.410
What's going on?

00:12:11.450 --> 00:12:14.650
Brother Godai broke
the window railing.

00:12:16.770 --> 00:12:18.920
What're you doing here?

00:12:20.790 --> 00:12:23.260
Why didn't you just
tell us you were back?

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:26.150
I tried!

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:27.500
Did you hear him?

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:30.900
I was sound asleep.

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:32.240
Me, too.

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:34.510
You know..

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:37.570
Anyway, you can
come in for tonight.

00:12:43.550 --> 00:12:45.390
After you fix that.

00:13:04.870 --> 00:13:05.630
Yes?

00:13:07.910 --> 00:13:09.440
Why, hello.

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:11.370
Hello, Mrs. Chigusa.

00:13:11.590 --> 00:13:13.510
Sorry to bother you again.

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:15.280
No problem.

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:16.820
Thanks for coming again.

00:13:17.420 --> 00:13:18.540
Kyoko!

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:21.270
It's Godai!

00:13:25.790 --> 00:13:28.750
I'm sorry.
She's still cranky.

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:32.020
Well, I'll be back
some other time.

00:13:32.300 --> 00:13:33.360
I'm sorry.

00:13:33.610 --> 00:13:34.230
It's okay.

00:13:34.300 --> 00:13:37.030
Good-bye.
See ya, Soichiro.

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:46.610
You're so stubborn!
It's been five days.

00:13:46.820 --> 00:13:48.480
Why don't you at least
hear him out?

00:13:49.780 --> 00:13:50.950
Stay out of it.

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:54.380
Kyoko!

00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:11.870
There's nothing
to talk about,

00:14:13.350 --> 00:14:14.970
no matter how many times
he comes to get me.

00:14:26.860 --> 00:14:29.140
I wonder how long
he'll do this?

00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:33.830
Hello. It's been
a long time.

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:36.330
I'm sorry to show up
at such short notice.

00:14:37.130 --> 00:14:38.470
How can I help you?

00:14:38.710 --> 00:14:40.250
well...

00:14:42.580 --> 00:14:46.800
Kyoko tells me that she wants
to quit her job as the manager.

00:14:48.140 --> 00:14:51.480
So suddenly?
Is there a reason?

00:14:53.010 --> 00:14:57.270
Actually, she's
already come home.

00:14:58.150 --> 00:14:59.120
Home to you?

00:15:00.200 --> 00:15:03.690
She says she doesn't wish
to go back to Maison Ikkoku.

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:05.490
I see.

00:15:07.030 --> 00:15:08.550
That's too bad.

00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:11.830
I'll be back with
her another day

00:15:11.900 --> 00:15:13.520
so she may speak
to you in person.

00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:20.070
It's only been five days
since the manager left,

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:23.080
but it's become so hard
to walk through here.

00:15:23.590 --> 00:15:27.210
Yeah. What a pain.

00:15:28.960 --> 00:15:31.380
Why is it such
a mess around here?

00:15:31.750 --> 00:15:34.620
I can't wait until
the manager comes back.

00:15:39.530 --> 00:15:42.390
Too bad!

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:46.610
Working overtime?

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:49.420
Yeah.

00:15:50.820 --> 00:15:54.980
Does that what's-his-name
still come here?

00:15:55.510 --> 00:15:58.270
Yes. Every day.

00:15:58.780 --> 00:16:01.250
Something must have
happened between them.

00:16:01.380 --> 00:16:03.400
Why do you look so happy?

00:16:04.520 --> 00:16:06.620
How dare he stalk
our daughter!

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:08.850
Kyoko obviously
doesn't like that.

00:16:09.730 --> 00:16:14.190
I wonder? She's always home
when Godai comes by.

00:16:14.570 --> 00:16:16.470
She's actually waiting
for him, you know.

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:18.440
Don't make
silly assumptions!

00:16:19.340 --> 00:16:22.500
There they go again.
They don't know anything.

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:26.710
He's a jerk!

00:16:30.860 --> 00:16:32.690
I never proposed to her!

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:35.110
She misunderstood me, and...

00:16:36.590 --> 00:16:38.010
I'm not falling for that!

00:16:46.700 --> 00:16:52.890
Shall I give him
a little time tomorrow?

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:01.740
We've accumulated
quite a bit

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:05.180
It's just a matter of time
before it reaches the ceiling!

00:17:05.550 --> 00:17:10.720
Humans are amazing. We can
adapt to any environment.

00:17:10.780 --> 00:17:12.300
Wherever I hang
my hat is home.

00:17:13.350 --> 00:17:17.160
Godai! Stop wasting
your time and drink!

00:17:19.860 --> 00:17:22.430
Why don't you
give me a hand?

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:24.590
Who do you think
made this mess?!

00:17:24.800 --> 00:17:27.030
The root of this
problem is you, isn't it?

00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:29.560
Hurry up and bring
back the manager.

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:31.030
You're so pathetic.

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:32.880
How can you go there
five days in a row

00:17:32.950 --> 00:17:34.270
and not make any progress?

00:17:37.720 --> 00:17:39.150
Hello.

00:17:39.720 --> 00:17:40.980
Mr. Landlord!

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:43.300
What're you doing here?

00:17:44.320 --> 00:17:45.920
I'm a penniless man.

00:17:47.050 --> 00:17:51.460
This is worse than I imagined.

00:17:53.290 --> 00:17:55.630
What? A new manager?

00:17:56.670 --> 00:17:58.050
I better hire one quickly

00:17:58.140 --> 00:18:01.700
or this place won't be
fit for human habitation.

00:18:01.880 --> 00:18:03.640
I'll be okay.

00:18:04.150 --> 00:18:08.800
Hold your horses. She's
just a temporary runaway.

00:18:09.450 --> 00:18:10.470
Runaway?

00:18:10.780 --> 00:18:13.770
Did she tell you herself
that she's quitting?

00:18:14.930 --> 00:18:16.450
No, her father did.

00:18:16.520 --> 00:18:19.010
I knew it.
She wouldn't quit

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:24.750
Is there a reason
behind this?

00:18:26.060 --> 00:18:27.020
Sort of.

00:18:31.800 --> 00:18:34.640
It is mighty inconvenient

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:36.900
that we don't know
when she's coming back.

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:41.910
messy space can
have its own charm.

00:18:42.420 --> 00:18:43.770
What charm?

00:18:44.810 --> 00:18:49.330
What say you hire
a temporary manager?

00:18:49.890 --> 00:18:50.750
Temporary?

00:18:51.350 --> 00:18:53.840
It's not that easy.

00:18:54.790 --> 00:18:57.280
I know a perfect candidate.

00:18:59.170 --> 00:19:00.960
He's a poor man,

00:19:01.030 --> 00:19:03.520
but his only job is part-timing
at a cabaret at night.

00:19:03.600 --> 00:19:06.500
He has nothing
to do during the day.

00:19:07.270 --> 00:19:07.900
Yeah!

00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:08.500
I know!

00:19:09.100 --> 00:19:09.790
No.

00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:15.470
Please.

00:19:15.540 --> 00:19:18.670
Not me, please.

00:19:44.340 --> 00:19:45.560
Where is he?

00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:48.100
It's about time he shows up.

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:50.300
Yes?!

00:19:55.280 --> 00:19:57.150
Coming!

00:19:59.290 --> 00:20:03.050
Right. I better
at least hear him out.

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:15.830
He's so persistent.
I turned him away.

00:20:18.920 --> 00:20:20.100
How dare you-

00:20:20.220 --> 00:20:21.710
Newspaper subscription.

00:20:23.750 --> 00:20:25.710
Godai's late today.

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:29.800
So you've decided
to see him?

00:20:31.400 --> 00:20:32.190
Why would I?!

00:20:35.970 --> 00:20:38.080
I don't care if he shows up.

00:20:41.100 --> 00:20:42.470
Chigusa residence.

00:20:43.170 --> 00:20:44.000
Father?

00:20:45.440 --> 00:20:46.860
Yes, this is Kyoko.

00:20:47.210 --> 00:20:50.030
How did you know
I was here?

00:20:50.650 --> 00:20:54.040
Yesterday, your
father came to see me.

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:55.770
My Father?

00:20:56.010 --> 00:21:03.440
Yes. I heard you want to
quit your job as manager.

00:21:03.520 --> 00:21:05.190
It's too bad.

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:09.600
What do you mean?
I never said such a thing.

00:21:09.760 --> 00:21:11.810
But you've already
gone home.

00:21:12.760 --> 00:21:14.490
That's because..

00:21:15.030 --> 00:21:16.580
My mother suddenly fell ill!

00:21:16.830 --> 00:21:18.760
Whose mother
suddenly fell ill?

00:21:19.830 --> 00:21:20.790
Shut up!

00:21:21.270 --> 00:21:23.360
This is an important call!
Stay out of it!

00:21:24.040 --> 00:21:26.980
But I'm not sick at all!

00:21:27.040 --> 00:21:28.640
Just get out of here!

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:29.760
Whatever!

00:21:32.350 --> 00:21:36.110
E-Excuse me.
In any case, father, I...

00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:41.150
Kyoko, it's all right.

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:48.690
I'm grateful that
you've lasted this long.

00:21:49.360 --> 00:21:53.430
Anyway, I've already
hired a new manager,

00:21:54.540 --> 00:21:57.300
although he's
a temporary one.

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:03.330
What? A new manager?

00:22:04.310 --> 00:22:07.150
Hello? Are you there, Kyoko?

00:22:07.490 --> 00:22:08.380
Hello?

00:22:09.520 --> 00:22:10.960
Y-Yes.

00:22:11.160 --> 00:22:15.550
So don't you worry a thing
about Maison Ikkoku.

00:22:16.260 --> 00:22:20.430
Thank you. Good-bye.

00:22:24.440 --> 00:22:28.460
I lost a place
to go back to...

00:22:38.920 --> 00:22:42.270
I don't have time to go
to the manager's place today.

00:22:42.520 --> 00:22:44.720
Hey! I can see the floor!

00:22:44.820 --> 00:22:48.050
We can party
in comfort again!

00:22:50.670 --> 00:22:53.900
Hey! Partying is not
allowed in the hallway!

00:22:54.330 --> 00:22:57.780
C'mon! It's a party for you.

00:22:57.910 --> 00:22:58.590
For me?

00:22:59.070 --> 00:23:01.530
Let's raise our
drinks to Godai

00:23:01.600 --> 00:23:03.360
for his new position
as the manager!

00:23:03.480 --> 00:23:04.860
Cheers!

00:23:05.770 --> 00:23:06.750
you...!

00:23:06.840 --> 00:23:08.000
Uncle.

00:23:09.510 --> 00:23:11.840
...when's Manager coming back?

00:23:12.350 --> 00:23:14.410
Why don't you go get her?

00:23:14.780 --> 00:23:18.240
But before you do, can you
fix the leak in my ceiling?

00:23:18.700 --> 00:23:21.780
And there's no more toilet
paper on the second floor.

00:23:22.020 --> 00:23:23.490
And can't you do
something about the floor

00:23:23.560 --> 00:23:24.960
in the laundry drying area?

00:23:25.170 --> 00:23:28.610
Isn't it convenient to
have a manager around?!

00:23:31.030 --> 00:23:32.010
It's great!

00:23:35.300 --> 00:23:39.560
Manager, I'm coming
to get you tomorrow!

00:23:49.630 --> 00:23:51.120
Love hotel?!

00:23:51.360 --> 00:23:53.470
We only came out! That's it!

00:23:53.570 --> 00:23:55.330
You came out
because you went in.

00:23:55.400 --> 00:23:56.910
What the hell
have you done?

00:23:57.040 --> 00:23:59.600
After the manager finally
decided to come back?

00:23:59.840 --> 00:24:03.450
Next: Kyoko's Big Shock!
Akemi and Godai Together?!

00:24:03.540 --> 00:24:05.400
But it's the truth!
